# Cita del SOFTWARE (servidor MCP y skills). Para los DATOS se cita el conjunto de cada país con su DOI:
# la herramienta how_to_cite del servidor devuelve la cita formateada.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. If you use the data of a country,
  cite that country's ParlaIbero dataset with its DOI as well.
type: software
title: "ParlaIbero tools: MCP server and diaries-* pipeline skills"
abstract: >-
  An MCP server that gives AI agents access to the ParlaIbero corpora of plenary speeches from
  16 Ibero-American parliaments (Harvard Dataverse), and the Claude Code skills that built them
  from session diaries.
authors:
  - family-names: Rodrigues-Silveira
    given-names: Rodrigo
    affiliation: "Instituto de Iberoamérica, Universidad de Salamanca"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-03"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rodrodr/parlaibero-tools"
url: "https://rodrodr.github.io/parlaibero/"
keywords:
  - parliamentary speeches
  - legislative debates
  - Latin America
  - Spain
  - Portugal
  - MCP
  - corpus construction
references:
  - type: data
    title: "ParlaIbero: Parliamentary Speeches from Latin America, Portugal and Spain"
    authors:
      - name: ParlaIbero
    publisher:
      name: Harvard Dataverse
    url: "https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataverse/parlaibero"
    notes: "Collection. Each country is a dataset with its own DOI, authorship and version."
